     1	"""Deterministic scenario generation for the Monte Carlo runner.
     2	
     3	A `Scenario` is a JSON-serialisable snapshot: rover start poses + per-rover motor
     4	model, cube start poses, a random depot-corner-per-colour assignment, and the
     5	sensor/contact noise params for that run. `generate(seed, family)` is a pure
     6	function of its inputs (one `np.random.default_rng(seed)` consumed in a fixed
     7	order) -- same seed + family always yields the same scenario.
     8	
     9	Depot / start points follow the official convention (CONTRATO.md s3 example:
    10	(40.5,2.5)/(2.5,40.5)/(40.5,40.5) cells on a 43-cell field, start (2.5,2.5)):
    11	2.5 cells in from each edge of the corner, derived from `cfg.board.cols/rows` (not
    12	hard-coded), so a differently-sized board still gets sane points.
